## Standard screen frame (system-agnostic — keep)

`{{FRAME_W}}×{{FRAME_H}}` mobile frame. Bind bg to `{{PAGE_BG_TOKEN}}`. `clipsContent = true`.
`overflowDirection = "VERTICAL"` if content scrolls, otherwise `"NONE"`.

Chrome elements (Status Bar, Bottom Nav, Home Indicator) live at the **END** of the children list with
`numberOfFixedChildren` set to the count of chrome elements (it counts from the END — see
`skills/figma-gotchas.md` Gotcha #16).

```javascript
const screen = figma.createFrame();
screen.name = "Profile / Default";              // "<Flow> / <Screen>" — prefix drives section grouping
screen.resize({{FRAME_W}}, {{FRAME_H}});
bindFill(screen, tokens.pageBg);                // {{PAGE_BG_TOKEN}}
screen.clipsContent = true;
// ... build content first ...
// ... then append chrome at the END ...
screen.numberOfFixedChildren = 2;               // e.g. Status Bar + Home Indicator
screen.overflowDirection = "NONE";              // "VERTICAL" if the content scrolls
```

## Section organization (system-agnostic — keep)

Group related screens horizontally in a SECTION node, one section per flow:
- Section width = 80 padding + N × {{FRAME_W}} + (N−1) × 80 gap + 80 padding
- Section height = 80 + {{FRAME_H}} + 80
- Each screen at section-relative `(80 + i × ({{FRAME_W}} + 80), 80)` for `i = 0..N−1`
- `SECTION.appendChild` reinterprets x/y as section-relative — re-assign after appending (Gotcha #15).

(The `relayout` / `flow-layout` skill automates this — group by the flow prefix before the first " / ".)

## Scroll pattern (system-agnostic — keep)

- Screen frame: fixed `width/height` + `clipsContent = true`.
- Chrome at the END of children; `numberOfFixedChildren` = chrome count (counts from the end).
- `overflowDirection = "VERTICAL"` when content overflows, `"NONE"` otherwise.
- `scrollBehavior` does NOT exist in the current Plugin API (Gotcha #16).

## Layer / z-order (system-agnostic — keep)

Layer order is the children array order: first child renders at back, last at front. For overlays
(modals, tooltips), put the scrim mid-stack and the chrome (Status Bar, Home Indicator) at the top.

## Render-verify checklist (system-agnostic — keep)

1. `figma_get_component_image` on the new screen (never inline base64).
2. Verify: layout aligned, colors render (no purple "missing variable"), text wraps, no clipping,
   chrome at correct z-order.
3. **Binding audit (Gotcha #27)** on every NEW frame you built (not {{SYSTEM_NAME}} instance internals):
   non-white/black fills bound, non-zero radii → `Border-Radius/*`, non-zero padding/itemSpacing →
   `Scale/*`, every TEXT node has a `textStyleId`, visible stroke weights → `Border-Width/*`.
4. **Instance check** — every visible instance points to a published {{SYSTEM_NAME}} component, not a
   stale local/foreign main.

